<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="155" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Uploads filed to a CHILD record (to-do, event, contact, …) resolve the right container — the secure ancestor's own container when the parent is secure, else the record's business-unit container — instead of a misleading 409</title>
    <phase>Session 27 — UAC defect remediation (residual found by the task 151 verifier, 2026-10-01)</phase>
    <gate>startable after 151 (merged) — coordinate with 146 (child ownership) and 144 (named secure team)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes where file BYTES are stored for every upload filed to a non-securable record — an isolation surface (the #1038 class: a secure record's content landing in a shared container).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security isolation of file content; fail-closed decisions on an upload path; interacts with C10 child ownership.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits RecordContainerResolver.cs and the OBO record-keyed upload routes, which 151 just changed and 146 will consume.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>151</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, security, spe, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Task 151 adversarial verifier, 2026-10-01: "the misleading 409 'No storage container is configured' remains on the OBO record-keyed routes for any NON-securable entity". Owner directives: nothing deferred; "a secure record MUST always have at least one user who can see it"; C10 part 2 — children of a secure record are secure.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make an upload filed to a child record land in the correct storage container: the secure ancestor's own container when the record hangs off a secure project, matter or work assignment, otherwise the record's business-unit container — and never a misleading 409 for a record whose container is derivable.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer — SPE container resolution and the OBO record-keyed upload routes.</role>

  <goal>For PUT /api/obo/records/{entityLogicalName}/{recordId}/files/{*path} and POST …/upload-session, a record of a NON-securable entity (sprk_todo, sprk_event, contact, sprk_communication, sprk_invoice where not securable, …) resolves its container from data, never from the caller: if the record's core ancestor (project / matter / work assignment) is SECURE, the ancestor's own container (fail closed if that container is missing); otherwise the record's own owningbusinessunit container (the behaviour the two-argument overload already documents). An unresolvable ancestor or business unit refuses with a specific reason code; nothing ever falls back to a shared container for a record that might be under a secure root.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>THE DEFECT. `RecordContainerResolver.ResolveForRecordAsync` (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs:176-183) returns `SecureContainerDecision.Decide(isSecure: false, ownContainerId: null, fallbackContainerId: nonSecureFallbackContainerId)` for every NON-securable entity WITHOUT reading the record. The OBO record-keyed routes call the two-argument overload, which passes a null fallback and whose own documentation says the non-secure default is derived "from the RECORD's own owningbusinessunit" — but that derivation only happens on the SECURABLE path. So every upload to a to-do, event or contact through those routes resolves Unresolved and the route answers 409 "No storage container is configured" (OBOEndpoints.cs record-keyed handlers, ~:94-180 and ~:337-400), even when the record's business unit has a container.

THE ISOLATION HALF (why this is not just a usability fix). Owner C10 part 2 (BINDING): children of a secure record are secure. A to-do, event or communication filed under a SECURE project must have its file bytes in the secure project's OWN container — the #1038 class of leak (a secure record's content in a shared container) would otherwise reappear through the child record the moment the 409 is "fixed" naively by reading the child's business unit. The child's link to its root is the core-ancestor stamp (`CoreAncestorResolver`, tasks 050/052; `sprk_regarding{project|matter|workassignment}` columns, `CoreAncestorResolver.cs:56-92`); sprk_document has typed lookups instead (sprk_project / sprk_matter / sprk_workassignment).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="read">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/OBOEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="read">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="read">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/SecureContainerDecision.cs</file>
      <file role="read">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/CommunicationContainerResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/RecordKeyedUploadAuthorizationTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Fail closed (ADR-003): an unreadable ancestor link, an unreadable ancestor flag, or a secure ancestor with no container REFUSES (secure_record_container_missing / a new container_ancestor_unresolved code) — never a shared container.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">The container is derived from data only; the caller never names it (task 076's rule, "no client can name where bytes go").</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The two-argument overload keeps its documented meaning (non-secure default from the record's own owningbusinessunit); the four-argument overload with an explicit fallback (server ingest, e.g. Communication:ArchiveContainerId) is unchanged in behaviour for records with NO secure ancestor. CommunicationContainerResolver's securable-regarding loop must keep working — run its tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">One record read for the child (owningbusinessunit + its ancestor link columns) and at most one read of the ancestor (flag + container) — no per-upload metadata round trips beyond 151's single classification.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">ADR-038 test bans; prove each new branch bites by seeding.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Inventory which non-securable entities reach the OBO record-keyed routes (EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType keys: contact, event, todo, invoice, …) and, per entity, how it links to its core ancestor (sprk_regarding{core} columns vs typed lookups); verify the columns read-only against live metadata.</step>
    <step order="2">Extend the NotSecurable branch of the TWO-argument path: read the record's owningbusinessunit + ancestor link(s); if an ancestor is secure → that ancestor's own container (refuse if absent); if the record links to MORE than one secure root, refuse (ambiguous) — consistent with CommunicationContainerResolver's ambiguity refusal; else the record's business-unit container; Unresolved only when genuinely no container exists (and say so precisely).</step>
    <step order="3">Tests: a to-do under a SECURE project resolves the project's container; a to-do under a non-secure project resolves its own BU container; an event with no ancestor resolves its BU container; an unreadable ancestor refuses; a secure ancestor without a container refuses; two secure ancestors refuse; the four-argument ingest path is unchanged; drive at least one REAL route end-to-end (not the filter and resolver composed by hand — the 151 verifier's test-shape gap).</step>
    <step order="4">Update the resolver's comments (the NotSecurable branch currently says "nothing to read") and the route comments; record in notes.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A file uploaded through the real PUT /api/obo/records/sprk_todo/{id}/files/… route for a to-do whose core ancestor is a SECURE project is stored in that project's own container (asserted on the drive the route resolves).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The same for a to-do under a NON-secure project resolves the to-do's own business-unit container; no 409.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A record with no ancestor resolves its business-unit container; a business unit with no container still answers the documented 409 with precise copy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: unreadable ancestor link or flag → refusal with a reason code; secure ancestor without a container → secure_record_container_missing; two secure ancestors → ambiguity refusal. None resolves a shared container.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The four-argument (explicit fallback) path and CommunicationContainerResolver behave as before for records without a secure ancestor (existing tests green, unmodified assertions).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each new branch is proven to bite by seeding its removal; BFF unit + NetArchTest green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, existing non-admin test user, no relocation): upload a file to a to-do under the secure test project and confirm (read-only) the item lands in the project's container; upload to a to-do under an ordinary project and confirm its BU container.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a child entity reaching these routes has NO reliable link to its core ancestor (no sprk_regarding{core} stamp and no typed lookup), STOP and report the entity — do not guess an ancestor. Recommendation: refuse uploads for that entity until 146/147 give it a link.</trigger>
    <trigger>If CoreAncestorResolver's stamp can be stale (ancestor re-parented) in a way that would send bytes to the wrong root, STOP and report; do not paper over it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Upload to a to-do under a secure project">
      <steps>
        <step>As a non-admin test user shared on the secure test project, open a to-do filed under it and upload a file through the to-do's document control.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The upload succeeds (no "No storage container is configured" error) and the file is stored in the secure project's container, not a business-unit container.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>Residual of task 151 (#1038 hardening), found by its adversarial verifier on 2026-10-01; owner directives forbid deferral. Relates to C10 part 2 (tasks 144-149): 146 makes child OWNERSHIP follow the secure root; this task makes child CONTENT follow it. Session notes: notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md.</notes>

  <execution>
    <outcome>completed — with escalation trigger 2 FIRED for one part (child filed under another child), which is held fail-closed and awaits an owner decision. Branch task/uac-r2-155. Full write-up: notes/task-155-child-record-container-resolution.md.</outcome>
    <rigor>FULL (bff-api, security; .cs + tests/**). Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check run.</rigor>
    <summary>RecordContainerResolver: a CHILD record (sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_invoice) now reads its root links on its ONE record read; a SECURE root (project/matter/work assignment) decides — its own container, or secure_record_container_missing; two secure roots → container_ancestor_ambiguous; unreadable / missing root → container_ancestor_unresolved (503 / 409); otherwise the explicit fallback or the record's own owningbusinessunit container. A child type with unknown links (sprk_document, sprk_communication, sprk_analysis — no caller today) is refused (trigger 1 shape). A non-securable entity with no ancestor concept (contact, account) now honours the two-argument overload's documented business-unit derivation; with an explicit fallback it is unchanged (zero reads). SecurableEntityRegistry memoizes its catalog per scope so the root's securability question costs no second metadata round trip with Redis down. SpeFileStore.UploadSmallAsUserAsync (ConflictBehavior overload) made virtual for the end-to-end route test (existing facade idiom, no behaviour change). OBO route comments updated.</summary>
    <escalation-fired>Trigger 2: the sprk_regarding{core} value on a child filed under ANOTHER child (communication/event/invoice/document/analysis) is a denormalized stamp that is never refreshed when that intermediate is re-filed (one-hop by design) and survives a native form clear (task 051 F-051-6). Trusting it sends a secure root's bytes to a shared container. NOT papered over: such records are refused with container_ancestor_unverifiable (409) — on the OBO routes they were already 409; on Office save they previously fell through to the SHARED default container. Live dev: 13 of 50 to-dos and 1 of 73 events are in this shape. Owner options: (a) read the intermediate live (amends the read budget), (b) cascade re-stamp children on intermediate re-file (recommended — also fixes the access over-grant), (c) accept the refusal. Trigger 1 did NOT fire for the routes: todo/event/invoice links verified live; guard test pins it.</escalation-fired>
    <live-checks-read-only>spaarkedev1 2026-10-01: sprk_todo + sprk_event carry sprk_regarding{project,matter,workassignment,servicerequest} and child regardings; sprk_invoice has typed sprk_matter/sprk_project and NO sprk_regarding{core}; sprk_issecure exists on project/matter/workassignment/INVOICE, not on servicerequest/document/communication/analysis/agreement/budget/reportcard/organization; 1 secure project (own container), 0 to-dos under it, 0 secure invoices; 9 projects + 18 matters carry NULL sprk_issecure (so a NULL root flag is read as non-secure + logged, not refused).</live-checks-read-only>
    <behaviour-changes-outside-routes>OfficeService.ResolveContainerAsync: a to-do/event/invoice under a secure root now resolves to the root's container (or refuses) instead of the configured shared default; a contact target uses its BU container. CommunicationContainerResolver passes securable regardings only — sprk_invoice is securable live, so an email regarding an invoice under a secure matter now routes to the matter's container. Records with no secure root: unchanged.</behaviour-changes-outside-routes>
    <placement-and-justification>No new service, DI registration, endpoint, option, job or NuGet package. New surface is internal to the existing RecordContainerResolver: (1) Existing — RecordContainerResolver is THE record→container mapping (task 075); CoreAncestorResolver owns the child taxonomy and core lookup list, referenced (CoreAncestorLookups, IsChildRecordEntity) rather than restated. (2) Extension — extended in place; a separate resolver would create a second container mapping, which task 075 forbids. (3) Cost of doing nothing — every to-do/event/contact upload on the record-keyed routes answers a misleading 409, and an Office save to a to-do under a secure project lands in a shared container SPE cannot un-share (#1038 class). The nested ChildAncestorLinks table is static data verified against live metadata. Placement: stays in the BFF (Infrastructure/Dataverse) beside its only consumer path.</placement-and-justification>
    <tests>New: ChildRecordContainerResolutionTests (29), RecordKeyedUploadRouteChildRecordTests (4, real mapped PUT route end to end), SecurableEntityRegistryTests memo test (1), RecordContainerResolverTests.NonSecurableEntity_WithoutFallback_DerivesTheRecordsBusinessUnit (2). Changed (pinned the defect): RecordContainerResolverTests zero-read test moved sprk_invoice→contact (assertions unchanged); RealNonSecurableEntity_ResolvesAsBefore lost sprk_invoice and its no-fallback→Unresolved leg. Office fixtures answer the new non-securable owningbusinessunit read with an empty row (§F.2). Mutations M1–M10 each seeded, watched red, reverted.</tests>
    <manual-live-gates>Pending (no live writes this session): deploy BFF to dev; create a to-do regarding the secure test project 65a3fab2-77a5-f111-aaad-70a8a590c51c and upload via its document control as a non-admin shared user, then confirm read-only GET /drives/{the project's CURRENT sprk_containerid}/root/children (f5 correction: b!MVasATu_GE6Lqs6JOGaeghG_EVjnHABFpxLm1FYg2Ah7gIBcg3lNSbiHX5dqt_eN since the task-144 cutover re-provisioned the project on 2026-10-02; the id originally written here, b!HBRbokLXnUGzaDLSTdNFvM5RFHtaaUZCi0Jm-xs-hDQV_6QuLuKmR4jrMdC6UgMm, is an orphaned, empty drive); upload to a to-do under an ordinary project and confirm its owningbusinessunit container; confirm a to-do filed under a communication answers 409 container_ancestor_unverifiable with nothing written.</manual-live-gates>
  </execution>

  <execution round="f1">
    <outcome>Adversarial-verifier findings closed on branch task/uac-r2-155-f1 (from task/uac-r2-155). AC4 and AC6 now met; AC7 remains PENDING-LIVE-GATE; escalation trigger 2 still awaits the owner's (a)/(b)/(c) choice.</outcome>
    <changes>
      (3/19, AC4) RecordContainerResolver: for a CHILD entity, a non-not-found failure reading the child's own row (its ancestor LINK) is now refused as container_ancestor_unresolved 503 (the same code and status as an unreadable root), logged with the fault. It is no longer a raw exception that the record-keyed routes rendered as a generic 500 "Upload failed: {ex.Message}". Not-found (404 container_record_not_found) and the resolver's own refusals pass through unchanged. A non-child keeps its propagate-raw contract.
      (4/20) Test: the registry classifies sprk_project as NotAnEntity → refusal 409, with no project read and no BU read, on both overloads.
      (5/20) Test: a root read that returns a null row → refusal 409, with no BU read, on both overloads.
      (6) IncomingCommunicationProcessor: the skip catch now uses a new internal static predicate, IsPermanentContainerRefusal. It adds container_ancestor_ambiguous, container_ancestor_unverifiable and container_ancestor_unresolved at 409 as PERMANENT skips. container_ancestor_unresolved at 503 stays transient and propagates, so the status code separates the two cases. Pre-existing codes are unchanged (pinned: container_record_not_found 404 and securable_entities_unknown 409 still propagate). New tests drive the REAL CommunicationContainerResolver over the REAL RecordContainerResolver. Cases: an email regarding an invoice under a secure matter → the matter's container. An invoice with no secure root → the archive, as before. An invoice under two secure roots → ambiguous, classified permanent. A missing root → 409, permanent. An unreadable root → 503, transient. The CommunicationContainerResolver exception docs now list the ancestor codes.
      (9) A route-level test for the documented 409 copy: an event with no ancestor whose BU has no container gets "No storage container is configured" plus the BU detail, and no bytes move.
      (2/18) The stale CoreAncestorResolver remarks (in two places) that said "sprk_todo has no sprk_regardingservicerequest" are corrected. The column exists live (verifier read-only check, 2026-10-01). The example is now sprk_invoice, which has no sprk_regarding{core} at all. This is a comment-only change.
      Route and resolver comments: the 503 now also covers "the child's own row could not be read".
    </changes>
    <not-changed-why>(13) Trigger 2 is held fail-closed and awaits the owner's choice of option (a), (b) or (c). (16) The taxonomy for agreement, budget, reportcard and organization belongs to tasks 146/147. (17) A Graph 403 for a user who can append to the to-do but has no SPE membership on the secure root's container is a membership-sync concern, not container resolution, so it is outside this task. (21) AC7: a live gate. There were no live writes.</not-changed-why>
    <placement-and-justification>No new service, DI registration, endpoint, option, job or package. IsPermanentContainerRefusal is a private catch filter promoted to an internal static method on the class that owns the catch, so the classification can be tested without driving Graph. Existing: the catch filter itself. Extension: extended in place. Cost of doing nothing: permanent 409 ancestor refusals enter the transient retry loop and lose the message capture.</placement-and-justification>
    <seeding>Each mutation was seeded, watched red, and restored. S1, child-row wrap disabled: 2 red (resolver 503 test, route 503 test). S2, wrap also swallows SdapProblemException: 1 red (child 404 test). S3, the verifier's seed (unknown root type → continue): 1 red. S4, the verifier's seed (null root → continue): 1 red. S5, predicate back to the original two codes: 5 red. S6, predicate ignores status: 2 red. S7, secure-root branch skipped: 26 red, including the communication → invoice → secure matter routing test.</seeding>
  </execution>

